WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.660
THE TIGER OF SPACE

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.300
"The Tiger of Space".

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:26.700
THE TIGER OF SPACE

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.130
The debris isn't that damaged. There may be survivors inside.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.130
I'll check it out.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.100
Please.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.260
Recon to Marbet's left, Üso.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.560
Shahkti and the others are getting further and further away.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.960
Why do I have to do this?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.130
Üso!

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.930
Sorry! I was just thinking about something!

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.030
I know you want to go save your friends,

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.300
but get it together, or you're going to get killed!

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.160
What's that light?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.800
There was a survivor?!

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.160
Miss Marbet!

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.500
H-Hold on!

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.730
He's flesh and blood...

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.330
Why are you hesitating?!

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.700
I can't shoot him!

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.560
Please, no! I surrender!

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.700
If you hadn't resisted...

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:46.360
If you hadn't resisted, even Miss Junko wouldn't have killed you!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.600
You had to have known that!

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.760
A meaningless death.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.960
If he'd stayed hidden a little longer, I could have saved him.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.960
Lt. Godwald, repairs on the Abigor will be finished, soon.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.730
Good. Have something to eat.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.230
Thanks for the food.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:41.200
Looks they're repairing the ship at the La Vie En Rose IV.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.130
If they had a dock like this, I wish the Aeneas could have come, too.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.800
I'm sure your sister and the others are all right.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.330
I hope so.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.160
If our families had survived, we'd want to be with them too.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.900
Are you saying something might've happened to the Aeneas?!

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.530
No, that's not what I meant!

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.760
Man, look at how close they're getting!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.260
D-Don't tease us!

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.330
Sorry. Actually, I came to tell you...

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.300
...that Jinn Jahannam's given this ship a new name!

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.230
He says it's now called the Reineforce Junior.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:20.200
Reineforce Junior?! He didn't give it any thought at all!

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.500
It's big.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.160
There are all kinds of debris collected here.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.630
I can't see how anyone would survive in this.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.700
Haro? That's Haro!

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.930
Ouch! Stop me!

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.730
Haro! I've been looking for you!

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.960
Picture, taken! Picture!

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:58.930
A picture?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.330
Karlmann, Suzy! Flanders, too!

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.000
Where did you take this?!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.960
Huh? What's that?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.400
This is the mobile suit I saw adrift!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.230
Is something like this foolish?

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.230
Kasarelia!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.730
Someone's there. Haro, come!

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.100
Where was Squid 1 headed?!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.700
If you tell me, I'll give you an easy death!

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:17.660
La... To the La Vie En Rose, but I don't know where it is!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.460
Are you a student soldier?

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.930
You mean a student who's serving in the military?

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.730
No, I'm not! I'm a regular kid!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:25.830
The hell you are!

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.660
We met once before.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:29.760
What?

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:31.300
I'm Üso from Kasarelia!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.400
That boy I met... What are you doing here?

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.800
I was made a pilot.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.200
What?!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.030
I thought I'd been rescued by a PCST pilot!

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:45.860
But you're an enemy pilot?!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.430
Just let me explain!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.530
Shut up!

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.700
It just happened! A lot of things happened to me!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.630
I ended up piloting the Victory!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.360
And I fight because the BESPA mobile suits keep attacking me!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.330
Kid, I'm gonna teach you the ironclad rule of soldiers who fight in space.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.260
It is...

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:10.600
When a chance to survive presents itself, never let it slip away!

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.230
If you understand that, then go!

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.430
Go!

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.200
Üso!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.600
Come on.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.100
Okay, let's go, pilot of the League Militaire.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.160
Now I see!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.600
He said he'd teach me the ironclad rule of soldiers, right?

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.630
It's fast!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.430
Even knowing you're Üso Ewin from Kasarelia,

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.260
you are now my target!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:04.230
Risking his life to teach me what it means to risk your life?!

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.400
Whether you can seize a chance or not...

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.060
...depends on your will!

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:19.460
Trying to lure me into a tight space? I can handle that!

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.200
He's switching to mobile suit combat?!

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.300
You're strong, but...

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.200
Üso!

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:45.460
Üso, you can't beat him on your own!

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.960
We've got two more chasing us!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.330
Junko! Üso!

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.060
Oliver! You came!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.800
Now it's three on three!

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.760
Where's Üso?! Did he head into the debris field?

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.600
In this place...

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.730
Why, you!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.600
Trans, now!

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.630
Üso! Dodge!

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:21.360
Beam wires?!

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.660
Dammit!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.030
What?!

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.030
I won't let you!

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.100
Trans!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.730
My controls are dead!

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:38.930
Lieutenant!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.630
You were too eager for success.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.830
Band, cover our retreat!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:53.660
Jamming waves!

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:54.800
Sneaky!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.960
Cut through it!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.760
They sent out a mobile armor?

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.230
If the enemy recovery team is right in front of us,

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.860
it means there are no more allied soldiers in this area!

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.330
Not one?

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:11.000
Right. Let's get back to the La Vie En Rose!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:15.130
We're leaving, Üso. Are your Boots okay?

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:17.760
They're fine.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.160
Lieutenant, they want us to rendezvous with the main fleet once we finish our recon.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.060
I don't let someone I've targeted just get away!

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.300
But...

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.560
Don't make me repeat myself!

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.660
Really?

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.300
We spoke in the wrecked ship.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.260
And you're sure that pilot's name is Godwald?

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.900
Yes, I'm sure of it.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:13.800
If his name is Godwald, he must be Godwald the Man-Eating Tiger.

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:15.030
Man-Eating Tiger?

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.930
He shows up in suits that can transform into mobile armors.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.360
Even among the BESPA pilots,

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:24.600
he's infamous for being the most vicious in combat.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.500
I'll admit he's strict, but...

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:28.400
But what?

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:31.430
He doesn't seem like a vicious man.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.200
He nearly killed you!

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.360
Nice job. I heard things got hairy out there.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.660
I was saved, thanks to Miss Junko and Mr. Oliver.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.930
That's teamwork. Don't worry about it.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:46.830
Right.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.030
Haro needs his batteries changed.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.460
Miss Junko!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.300
Oliver?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.060
Üso's getting too used to space combat.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:58.300
If we're not careful, something bad might happen.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.330
Thank goodness! Thank goodness!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.830
They look healthy.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.660
Suzy's smiling!

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.130
Is that girl Üso's sister?

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.200
His neighbor. Just his neighbor.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.960
If this was one of the ships in the Keilas Guilie Fleet,

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.660
she's been taken to the Zanscare homeland.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.800
Now what, Üso?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.330
Hey.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:38.930
Üso...

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.530
Going out?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:42.600
For a bit.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.560
You Hiland kids,

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:50.260
your parents' ship just entered Side 2 territory.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.360
We've got communications back with them?

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.300
You contacted the Aeneas?

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.630
Thank goodness!

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.430
Big brother!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.400
We'll see Dad and the others again!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:01.000
That's great news!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:01.860
Really!

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.030
Big Brother!

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.430
Don't cry.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.430
I'm sorry, you guys.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.800
S-Sorry. It's just us who are happy about this.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:16.630
What are you talking about?! I'm happy if everyone's happy!

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:19.230
Yeah, we share all the happy and sad times.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.500
You could probably catch up to the Aeneas in the Fishbone from here.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.500
That's right! If you want to do that, we'll help.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.530
Yeah, yeah!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.630
Thanks. We can use the help.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:29.900
Marbet!

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:30.930
Hm?

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.400
Miss Marbet? Miss Junko?

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:35.600
What?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.860
It's none of our business.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:39.960
So?

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:41.800
What's so funny?!

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.630
This whole deal with you.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:48.330
The way you don't realize you're too clingy with that kid.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.330
I could say the same about you!

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:53.000
I don't act that way... Because I'm not that way!

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:55.960
I can tell! You really like Üso!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.760
And you don't like him?!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.860
I don't dislike him, but...

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:11.530
Odelo, even if the Aeneas is at Side 2,

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.100
it doesn't mean this'll get you closer to Suzy and the others.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.200
As long as it gets us anywhere closer to them!

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:21.830
There are parts of Side 2 that aren't under the Zanscare Empire's control.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:26.360
If that's the case, then why were you guys left back at the Hiland?

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:30.660
My dad's company was probably pressured by Zanscare.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:31.630
I see...

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:33.800
Üso's getting into the Victory.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:34.930
Let me see.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:38.530
What?

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.400
What happened?

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.160
Going to Side 2, huh?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:45.300
J-Just for a bit, to guard Tomáš and the others in the Fishbone.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.430
Yeah, right!

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:50.530
And maybe check on enemy ship movements, while I'm at it!

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:53.460
Even if you go after them, there's no guarantee that the ship...

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.760
...Shahkti and the others are on has returned to the homeland!

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.330
Uh-oh. I thought we could relax because they were arguing.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.700
Üso's really bad at lying, huh?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.230
Should we take 'em from behind?

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:05.330
Let's wait a little longer and see what happens.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.800
I'm going to collect information about the Zanscare Empire!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.130
Are you stupid?! Who do you think you are?!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.130
What can you do on your own...

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.730
...once you're separated from the Fishbone?!

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.630
Shahkti, Suzy, Flanders and Karlmann are there!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.200
I have to look for them! I have to go!

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.830
The turtle comes out of his shell.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.430
Miss Marbet?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.300
You hopeless kid.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.830
Miss Marbet... Miss Junko...

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.700
I'm sorry!

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.930
Debris field sighted ahead.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.660
It's space colony wreckage.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.800
Can we avoid it?

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.230
Hang on.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.430
What's that?

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:00.860
A friendly signal.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.830
One of ours? A civilian ship?

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.030
You don't think it's...

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.700
The Aeneas! The ship Dad and the others are on!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.560
Mom and the others came to meet us!

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.400
Üso, the Aeneas is at 10 o'clock!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.230
I can't see it yet on the Gundam's monitor,

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.430
but that's great, everyone! Congratulations!

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.860
Tomáš! Engines full! Run for it!

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:36.130
We're so close to being with Dad and the others!

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.130
Everyone, get away from me! I'm using the cannons!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.460
Hm... So, you've upgraded your weapons?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.130
Band! Trans! Flank him! The white Sinope can wait.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.030
Roger! Roger!

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.260
Hide in that large debris!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.000
I'm hiding us in the debris!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.600
Roger! 11 o'clock, dead ahead!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.030
Not bad.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.930
Damn these things! They've made the wires stronger!

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.760
I'll separate the Boots!

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:26.230
What?! He's docking-out?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.060
That's my target! Leave him to me!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:49.200
If Tomáš and the others meet up with the Aeneas and abandon the Fishbone,

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.500
Mr. Godwald probably won't attack the Aeneas!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.560
There's more small debris showing up!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.730
You can't escape! Your speed is no match for the Abigor's!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.460
I gave you a chance to survive once before! You won't get a second!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.100
Even if you're just a kid, so long as you choose this path,

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.260
you must accept your fate!

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:21.760
Drink your fill of the fear my comrades knew, and then die!

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:29.030
That's all? That's all the pressure this enemy pilot can give?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:36.500
You have to be a talented soldier to survive on the battlefield!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.130
Then I'll try to survive, Mr. Godwald!

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.760
His mobile armor can't enter a space this small!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:52.860
I'll draw him out!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.660
Trans, block his escape route!

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:04.430
That's right, if he can transform into a mobile suit, this won't be a problem for him!

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.230
Here it comes!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:09.330
What?!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:18.960
What? Was he leading me on?! Not bad!

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.760
I can't just run forever! Either I get him, or he gets me!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.860
Where are the Boots?!

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:30.630
The Boots should be around here!

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.130
I know you're hiding in here!

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.800
His Boots?!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.960
He's taken my front!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:52.360
I took the front! From Mr. Godwald!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.730
Kasarelia.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.300
What are you doing?!

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:58.800
If you don't shoot me this instant, you'll die!

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.200
Die!

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:11.030
You have no right to be a soldier!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.300
Üso, I know you can use that fuel tank for something!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:20.300
Üso!

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:21.700
You can do it!

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.830
You're finished!

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.630
Damn you!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:37.030
I'm gonna do this! I'll show you I can!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.160
I... I got him.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:47.430
What?!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.830
He ejected. He escaped...

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:56.060
I'm not dead yet. It'll take more than that!

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.000
W-What?!

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:00.500
I'll take this mobile suit!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:02.230
Oh, yeah?

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.830
You did it, kid!

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.100
I heard him...

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:23.500
At the very end, Mr. Godwald praised me.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:31.430
That's why... That's why fellow pilots,

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:35.000
when they face each other as foes, they end up like this!

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:46.230
It doesn't have to be this way!

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.800
Üso, do you read me? Thanks to you, we could rendezvous!

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.700
Thank you! We all owe you one!

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.530
Really? That's great.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.730
Warren, Karel, everything okay on your end?

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:02.730
Yeah. If you're okay, then let's get out of here.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:04.200
Roger.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.460
We need to find Shahkti and the others.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.500
We have to hurry!

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:38.400
In order to bring Martina to a doctor when she falls ill,

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:42.600
Üso and the others must infiltrate a Zanscare colony.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:48.660
There, Üso encounters a huge mobile suit that he's never seen before.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:53.400
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:56.500
Next Episode INFILTRATING ZANSCARE
"Infiltrating Zanscare".

00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:58.330
Please watch it!

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:59.460
Next Episode INFILTRATING ZANSCARE
